--- a document that loads
nodes=24
screen: name=fixture rect=200x160 name "root" is gone=true
named: go=3 off=4 icon=5 view=6 cells=7
kinds: go=3 off=3 cells=5
button go: text=GO rect=10,70
button off: enabled=false text=OFF
label: name=(anonymous) text=HELLO & GOODBYE palette=1 align=1
sprite: index=3 custom: payload=7
grid: rect=64x64 children=16
cell[1]: rect=76,100 payload=1
--- clicks on the loaded screen
bound=true
click(50,82) on GO: action=2 payload=0 leaf=go
click(100,124) cell row1 col2: action=1 leaf payload=6
click(150,5) on the panel: action=-1 node=none leaf=(anonymous) payload=0
click(250,150) outside: action=-1 node=none leaf=none payload=0
--- documents that do not load
line 1: unterminated <screen>
line 1: the root element must be <screen>, not <window>
line 1: no element
line 1: unterminated comment
line 1: attribute name needs a quoted value
line 1: unknown entity &nope; in attribute name
line 2: attribute rect written twice
line 2: `line` is the reader's own attribute
line 3: </screen> closes <panel>
line 1: text after the root element
line 1: no element <blink>
line 1: <panel> has no attribute colour
line 1: <panel> needs a rect="x,y,w,h"
line 1: no palette "loud"
line 1: <label> needs content or a text="..."
line 1: <grid> 30x30 does not divide into cells of 16
line 1: <grid> needs a name - its listener binds to it
line 1: the name "x" is already used
line 1: <screen> needs a positive width and height
line 1: <custom> needs a name - the app paints it by name
--- the stack
size=1 top=menu
push a game screen: size=2 top=game paintBase=1
the top screen's window: 200x120
a write through the stack's top, read through the app's handle: 12
pop -> true size=1 top=menu
pop the last -> false size=1
a translucent overlay on the menu: paintBase=0
an opaque dialog on top: paintBase=2
dialog closed: paintBase=0
